 !!! Note
     The minimum last stake amount can be configured using `last_stake_amount_min_ratio` - which defaults to 0.5 (50%). This means that the minimum stake amount that's ever used is `stake_amount * 0.5`. This avoids very low stake amounts, that are close to the minimum tradable amount for the pair and can be refused by the exchange.
 
+#### Currency exposure limit
+
+If you trade several pairs that are all priced against, or backed by, the same underlying currency (a handful of BTC-margined futures, or several pairs all quoted in the same stablecoin), a large adverse move in that one currency can hit several open trades at once. `max_currency_exposure` limits how much of your tradable capital may be committed at any one time to open trades sharing the same underlying currency - the quote currency for spot/margin pairs, or the settlement currency for futures contracts.
+
+Assuming a tradable balance of 1000 USDT and `max_currency_exposure=0.5`, at most 500 USDT may be committed across all currently open trades quoted in USDT. If ETH/USDT and BTC/USDT trades are already open with 300 USDT committed between them, a new trade in XRP/USDT requesting 400 USDT would be reduced to 200 USDT - the remaining room under the limit. If the limit is already fully used, the new trade is skipped entirely (stake amount of 0).
+
+This is not configured by default, i.e. no currency exposure limit is applied.
+
+!!! Note
+    This check applies identically whether running live, in dry-run, or in backtesting - it's evaluated as part of the same stake-sizing logic used by `max_open_trades` and `stake_amount`.
+
 #### Static stake amount
 
 The `stake_amount` configuration statically configures the amount of stake-currency your bot will use for each trade.
